WEBVTT

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.190
All right.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.990
No outs. Runner on first.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.580
First batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Kawashima.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:42.950
Ready!
First batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Kawashima.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:45.620
Stay focused.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.710
He'll start swinging from the first pitch!

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.170
A ball first?

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.380
A fastball.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:55.050
Ball!

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.170
99.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.890
Even though it was close, he saw through it.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.510
He pretended to swing and stopped.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.600
Kou's so thorough.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.560
Next is...

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.640
It's scary that he's aiming to hit,

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.310
but I want to get to an even count.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.730
A strike. Then...

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:12.110
A curveball.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.780
The one I threw in his second at-bat was to the outside corner.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:15.940
This time it'll be inside.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.780
It's okay. I won't get hit!

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.250
That was his 100th pitch.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.580
How's his condition?

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.920
Second batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Ishikawa.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.750
I'd know if I could just catch one pitch!

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.260
Ready!

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.180
Here it comes. Mizutani, come forward.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:40.550
Okay!

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:45.720
I got it!

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.930
Third base won't work?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:48.640
Out!

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.060
Tajima, thanks.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.110
Yeah. Although it was my ball just now.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.020
Third batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Yano.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:55.780
Ready!

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.690
Third batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Yano.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.400
This batter's already scored two runs.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.780
The next one's scored three.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.780
They won't try a squeeze here.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.740
Go ahead and put one in!

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.580
A strike.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.540
Please... don't hit it!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:14.710
Strike!

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.710
He counted my swing.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:17.670
Nice pitch!

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.340
Thank goodness!
Nice pitch!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:18.600
Thank goodness!

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.800
It's pretty clear that was inside. Sloppy.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.050
Is he waiting for a fastball? The next is a ball.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.890
Put in... some strength!

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:28.680
Ball!

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.150
What's with that? It was good pitch this time, but he let it pass?

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.440
The ninth inning's been full of fastballs.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.940
The sign... a strike.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.110
I'll bet it's the curveball I swung at and missed in my second at-bat.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.820
A curveball... in a difficult spot!

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.200
Shit!

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.200
The eighth run!

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:46.780
Just one run?

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:47.120
Nice batting!

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:47.410
The ball's slow, so it doesn't carry far.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.450
Nice batting!

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:49.250
The ball's slow, so it doesn't carry far.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.620
I told you to hit a sacrifice bunt!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.670
Ah, that's right! Crap!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.840
The score... The runs we made in the eighth inning...

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.090
Something's wrong.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.430
Why are they hitting everything all of a sudden?

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.550
Tajima!

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.550
Um...

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.850
Time out, please!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:09.560
Time!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.940
We don't have a messenger right now, so can I return to the bench?

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.860
All right. I'll allow it.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.690
Thank you!

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.730
Coach, something's off!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.400
What do you mean?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.700
Um, maybe it's the pitch or, well, the location.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.030
I mean, it's scary how accurately they're hitting the ball.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.620
It kind of feels like they're reading my mind.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:35.670
If they are, it's my mind they're reading, not yours.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.210
The dugout is easily visible from the other side.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.800
Maybe they've figured out our signs.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.010
Then, if we change our signs...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:45.380
Instead, isn't it about time for you to start calling the pitches, Tajima?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.100
Of course, that's with Mihashi's cooperation.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.640
He's thrown for more than three rotations now,

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.930
so he should have a better feel for the batters than you.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.150
Make sure to tell Mihashi to shake off the pitches he doesn't like.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:56.690
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.150
Good work.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.490
Hey, guys. From now on, I'll be calling signs without Coach Momo.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.030
It's better that way.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.740
And Mihashi. Shake off the signs you don't like.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.950
Sh-Shake...

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:09.450
What?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.660
Huh?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.580
Now that you mention it, have you ever shaken off a sign, Mihashi?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.840
I have!

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.670
I started shaking some off earlier.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.330
I see. Then, I'm counting on you.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.130
Yeah.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.340
All right! Let's change the flow of the game!

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.380
Yeah!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.210
Take it easy!

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:23.590
Yeah.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.590
Let them hit it.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.090
Yeah.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.590
Well, he wasn't forbidden to shake off signs or anything.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.560
It just means that he was happy with Abe's pitch selection.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.260
Now, we've got a three-run lead, but...

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.020
Thank you!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:33.350
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Wada.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:34.680
Now, we've got a three-run lead, but...

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.140
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Wada.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.110
I can hit it as I please, right? Yes!

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.110
Batter!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.230
Yes!

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.200
As I thought, a strike on the first pitch is scary.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:47.660
A curveball...

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.410
Ball!

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.950
She isn't signaling anymore.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.830
They noticed surprisingly fast.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.290
We'll put it in next.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.000
A shoot down low.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.710
Next is a strike, right?

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.840
Kou and Yano have both hit curveballs in this inning,

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.920
so they'll hone in on fast breaking balls.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.420
If it's a fastball, then I'll take a cut.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.640
Don't give away any more hits!

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.050
Lightly...

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.730
Second homer!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.850
Three runs!

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:29.660
In the fertile green fields, the light shines.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:37.910
We gather in the garden of learning,

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:44.130
as companions, without hesitation.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.210
11-5.
as companions, without hesitation.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.470
Time to lay the foundation for virtue.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.630
They really got us.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:50.340
Time to lay the foundation for virtue.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.260
Yeah.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.260
Are you okay?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:52.890
Time to lay the foundation for virtue.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:55.470
I'm... okay.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:55.810
Time to lay the foundation for virtue.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.270
Let's give it our all!

00:06:59.270 --> 00:06:59.940
Yeah!

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.440
Shit, I can't even apologize.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.360
Fifth batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Miyata.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.400
I'll go with the pitch Mihashi wants to throw most at a time like this.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.360
A slider low and outside.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:10.320
Ball!

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.910
Huh? It went out!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.490
Nice pitch! It was close!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.950
A high fastball down the middle!

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.040
Ball!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.750
Why'd you let it get to 2-0?
He'll go after the next pitch.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.790
A fastball's no good either?

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:24.000
What's good? If you don't like the sign, shake it off!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.670
An inside shoot.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:26.630
Ball!

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.380
It's not Tajima.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.380
Is Mihashi shaken up?

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.300
Mihashi. Straight down the middle is fine. Here!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.230
Ball! Ball four!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.020
It won't go in.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.360
Mihashi! Let them hit it.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.310
Leave it to the guys behind you!

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.150
Let them hit it!

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:47.320
Bring it on!

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.780
Sixth batter. Pitcher: Number 9, Kashima.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.030
That's what Abe tells me when I'm floundering.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.570
A fastball down the middle.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:54.870
He should be able to get him out after letting him hit.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.870
But if you're scared, then shake it off.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.540
A fastball down the middle. I can throw that.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.500
I have to catch it here.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.000
For sure!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:04.420
Second!

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.290
Yes!

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:14.220
I'm sorry!

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.300
It's okay!

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.390
It's nerves. Sakaeguchi, and me too.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:22.350
I'm nervous because Abe isn't here...

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.480
Sakaeguchi as well, because Abe isn't here.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.110
Is it because of Abe?

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:32.570
Mihashi, he means that if you can't pitch, it's natural that we'd lose.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.530
It's my fault.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.530
I need to speak up.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:48.960
One out!

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.710
Double play! Double play!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.590
I can make everyone calm down.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:58.180
If I'm okay, then everyone's okay.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:58.930
Seventh batter. First baseman: Number 3, Matsushita.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.220
I'm the ace.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:01.640
Ready!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.100
A fastball is fine.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.940
I'm all right.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.150
I can get it!

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:11.480
Out!

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:13.780
Nice catch!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:14.450
Nice pitch!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.900
Two outs!

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:19.120
They got back on their feet? They're really tenacious.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.660
You can hit as you please here.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:20.740
Eighth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Kurata.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.000
Just put a lid on their coffin.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.500
It's my last at-bat.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:25.960
Ready!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.290
I'll swing so hard that you'll regret it!

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.800
Even with a six-run lead, he's totally serious.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:36.220
But if Mihashi is okay, we won't give up.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.680
I'll end it with this batter!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.930
Okay. 0-1!
Strike!

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:40.640
Nice pitch!

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.390
It was a fastball.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.350
Do you think I can't hit it?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.730
For some reason, this guy's really fired up.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:47.810
But I...

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.280
I won't give up either!

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.860
Considering the situation, should we go with a curve?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.870
After a fastball, he'll hit a curveball.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:02.660
No good?

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.700
Then one more fastball.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.000
Diagonally...

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.710
I-I shook him off!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.500
It's normal.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.470
A fastball low and outside.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:16.920
Outside?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.340
Strike!

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.260
We've got him into a corner!

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.930
Though I shook him off,
he gave me another sign right away.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.810
Tajima has a lot of plans.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.770
Going by the book, I should take another ball here, but...

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.230
Next is...

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.940
A ball.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.980
I always nodded my head to the first sign,

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:40.490
but if I'd shaken it off, Abe might've given me another sign too.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:41.490
Ball!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:42.450
Close!

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.580
He let the ball drift out.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.910
If so, then that was for show.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.710
Next, he'll put in a fastball.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.870
This time, I'll swing.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.880
If I hit it, I'll run through first base!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:53.380
Just think about running past the bag.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:54.840
In any case, I'll make it on base!

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.800
Pitcher, keep going! You've got him cornered!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.260
Mihashi, try hard. Everyone, defense!

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.340
I can hit it. Have confidence!

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.220
I'm going to settle things and say goodbye to baseball.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.930
For the decisive ball, I want to go with a fastball. What do you think?

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.230
If it's a fastball, I'll miss.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.650
If not a fastball, then what?

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.650
You don't want to?

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.610
Today, he's thrown some walks, after all.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.110
Then, how about the opposite way, with one more curveball?

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:19.570
A curveball. The same angle as before.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.320
If I shake him off, he still gives me another sign.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:27.330
If Tajima was hesitating over a fastball versus a curveball,

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:31.500
then it's as if he consulted with me just now.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.960
It's my job to shake off signs,

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.630
though I should've known that naturally.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:40.090
Before now, I always forced Abe to take all the responsibility.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.260
I've made a lot of mistakes, about everything.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:47.010
From now on, I'll try hard!

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:48.720
I stopped my swing!

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.930
It's just barely in. I hope you saw it, Ump!

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.230
Strike!

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:54.690
All right!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.530
Nice pitch!

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.860
Nice pitching!

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.910
I wasn't able to swing even once.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.580
My turn at bat is done. Have to shake it off.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.790
We still have to play defense!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.750
You little rascal!

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:13.750
Nice location!

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.630
Abe, you should probably take that off soon.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.710
Nice pitching!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:29.220
I-I gave up some hits.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.680
Right.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.900
You can't do anything about those hits anymore.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.650
We're still in the middle of a game.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.730
Don't relax just because you're finished with defense!

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.190
Yeah.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.070
Show some fighting spirit! Let's go!

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.530
Yeah!

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:49.580
Once the game is over,
I need to tell Abe a lot of things.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:53.540
We're not a battery if I just act scared and depend on him.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.000
Yoshito, finish things up!

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.710
Yes!

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.460
Takumi...

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.220
Shuuhei, you're in left field.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.010
Yes!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.720
Takeshi. Choose pitches to make them hit to left field.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.350
Huh?

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:13.430
It's all right. They'll end up hitting my pitches, so I'll let Shuuhei touch the ball.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.440
What's so funny about Yoshito giving up hits?

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.360
Makoto! When did we win?

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.530
Um, we haven't won yet.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:25.900
Then, don't go soft!

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:26.400
Yes, sir!

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.780
Finish them off with no more hits!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.620
We're taking this momentum into the sixth round!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.160
Yes, sir!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.000
Bijoudai Sayama High.
Announcing a change of players.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.380
Replacing the pitcher, Kashima, is Takenouchi.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.040
Replacing the left fielder, Takenouchi, is Moriya.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.130
It's because we worked so hard attacking in the eighth inning.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:41.710
Replacing the left fielder, Takenouchi, is Moriya.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:45.470
But then, you'd expect them to use their third pitcher, as usual.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.050
Maybe they're saving the last pitcher?

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.890
Oh well, there has to be a reason they're not playing him.

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:55.350
We got to their second pitcher,
but they can't use their third today.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.640
This is our lucky break!

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:59.690
Let's hit all the way around the order.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:00.730
We'll attack with everyone!

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:01.310
Yes!

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.570
We'll take back this game one run at a time!

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:06.070
Yeah!

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.740
We definitely won't give up!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.280
Yeah!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.240
We're going to win!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.450
Yeah!

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.450
You heard that, right?

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.620
The players are still energetic! Let's be energetic as well!

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.170
I'm asking for your loudest cheers yet today!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:20.830
Yeah!

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.840
You ohay?

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:24.050
Yesh, I'll try harg!

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.260
Bottom of the ninth inning.
Nishiura High to bat.
Ready!

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.060
I've had two good bunts.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.350
I should have a good grasp of the pitch locations.
Third batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Suyama.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:40.900
He's just come in. He should want to put in a strike on the first pitch.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.230
It's a fastball!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:43.860
Got it!

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:47.280
It got through!

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.070
Down the middle!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.110
Nice batting!

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:50.610
Yeah!

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:54.120
Looks like Saitou isn't the third pitcher today.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.120
Is he out of commission?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.910
Do you <i>have</i> to frown like that?

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:03.210
I can't even tell if he's trying to warn me about something.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.000
But he's up to something.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.460
Fourth batter. Catcher: Number 5, Tajima.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.510
If he wins this game,
he'll try it again in the next one.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.090
Fourth batter. Catcher: Number 5, Tajima.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:09.970
Ready!

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.590
In the third inning, with runners on first and third,

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.220
he got me out with three strikes.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:16.430
That was good pitching.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.520
One more like that would be nice.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.270
Even a better pitch would be okay.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.850
Whatever it is, I'll hit it.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:22.730
Bring it!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:24.770
Ball!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:26.730
He watched it pass with just his eyes.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.940
In this situation, he's totally lacking in childish charm.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.280
He's got a good physique and mental attitude.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.240
He's like a jewel. It's just a pain.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:37.200
But right now, what's important is to end the game with as few pitches as possible.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.500
A slider.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.910
Bring it! Bring it!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:43.710
A slider!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:48.840
Fair! Fair!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.220
Suyama, you can make it!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:15:59.720
No slide!

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:05.100
All right!

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.310
Nice, Suyama!
All right!

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.020
Take that!

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.570
Sorry.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:15.280
I thought it would cause trouble if he stuck around, so I let him hit it.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.530
It dropped in a lucky spot.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:19.370
We really let Shuuhei hit the ball.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.080
It'll be a long meeting again.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.500
You don't need to tell me that.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:27.380
Let's stop the last three batters quickly and cheer up the coach.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.550
Okay. Let's do it.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.170
Fifth batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Hanai.
Hanai! Follow up!

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.300
Yeah!

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.840
Before now I've only hit fastballs.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.760
I'll wait for a fastball this time too.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.720
I can't pop up. I have to get on base too.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:43.690
Strike!

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.020
The speed of his pitching has dropped?

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.940
I see. Is he holding back?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.230
Because it's the last inning with a five-run lead?

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:55.070
Shit. It's not over yet!

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:57.450
Strike!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.700
I fell for it!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.660
Nice pitch!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.870
Damn it.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.000
I'd better hit the next one!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.870
It's written all over your face.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:07.460
Well, there's a certain amount of charm to being a first year, I guess?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:08.420
We're not playing around.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:09.630
I'll hit it!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:13.590
Strike!

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.680
Fukami! Let's do the next one now!

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:19.300
Yeah.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.010
Three fastballs in a row.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:21.760
Okay.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:22.810
We're not done yet.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:23.270
Yeah.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.520
If I don't hit it... Next is...

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:30.400
Sixth batter. First baseman: Number 3, Oki.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.270
Ready!

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:35.490
During this guy's previous at-bat, he connected pretty well.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.950
Let's proceed carefully.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:40.620
Ball!

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:42.950
With one out, have you started thinking of the win?

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.330
You don't have to cut it that fine.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:46.910
Strike!

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.880
It'll be too late if we wait until we're cornered.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:52.840
Hit-and-run. All right. I'm heading for home.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.800
The next will be a fastball.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.970
Remember the previous at-bat and swing hard.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.760
With a hit-and-run, as long as I connect, Tajima will be able to advance.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:02.760
The direction doesn't matter.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.720
Hit hard and get on base!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.480
Are they going to make a move?

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.350
If they're up to something, now's the right time, considering the count.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.270
Based on the seventh batter's last at-bat,

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:14.150
if we get the sixth batter out, the game is essentially over.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.860
Don't you worry about it.
Just focus on the batter.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.240
Focus on the batter.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:22.660
He took off!

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:24.370
A fastball!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.540
He hit it!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:30.290
Out!

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:43.850
Seventh batter. Left Fielder: Number 10, Nishihiro.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.610
Nishihiro, you can do it!

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.520
Nishihiro! Nishihiro!

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.980
Swing as hard as you can!

00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:00.950
Nishihiro! Nishihiro!

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:06.620
Nishihiro! Nishihiro! Nishihiro!

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:10.330
I can hit it. I can hit it...

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:12.960
Strike!

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:13.540
Nice swing!

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.170
You'll hit it!

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:18.300
I'll hit... the next one.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:24.640
Nishihiro! Nishihiro! Nishihiro!

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.640
Strike!

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.600
One more!

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:34.610
Nishihiro! Nishihiro! Nishihiro!

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.480
Keep your eye on the ball!

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:40.440
Nishihiro, you can hit it!

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.450
Hit it. Please hit it!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.120
Strike!

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.420
All right!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:58.130
Let's go!

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:58.920
Yeah!

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:08.060
Bijoudai Sayama High wins!

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.470
Good game!

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.560
Let's go to the stands!

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:18.070
Yeah!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:35.540
Okay!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.210
Thank you for cheering us on!

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.420
Thank you!

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.260
Great job guys!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.130
We'll cheer for you again!

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.840
Big brother!
We'll cheer for you again!

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:54.560
Let's go back.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.960
Y-Your leg...

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:27.300
We lost.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.440
Okay. That's enough!

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:43.980
Today's game took your best effort. And we lost.

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:46.950
If only I'd hit more... If only I'd run faster...

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.910
If only I had more power... better technique...

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.660
Everyone's thinking that, right?

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:52.620
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:55.580
Then, don't let your frustration go to waste by crying it away!

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:59.250
That frustration is energy for improving yourself.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.090
Hold it inside carefully!

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:02.090
Yes, ma'am!

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.550
Now, gather all the gear.

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:06.130
Two weeks from now is the Newcomers Game.

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.220
And after that is the Fall Tournament.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:10.050
So let's hurry back and practice!

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.800
Yes, ma'am!

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:47.400
It's Nishiura High's first loss,

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:50.860
but we can't just sit around and mope.

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:58.040
Thinking positively and facing our next goal, we'll make a new start.

00:23:58.240 --> 00:24:01.750
For that purpose, our team's goal is...

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:03.710
Next time:

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:05.170
Starting Again.

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:09.130
Everyone on the team has a good appetite.
